   "style": "h2",
   "markDefs": [],
   "children": [
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "fe72ddb1ee58",
     "text": "Is Animal Kingdom Good for Kids?",
     "marks": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "_type": "block",
   "_key": "fd42e4dddc76",
   "style": "normal",
   "markDefs": [],
   "children": [
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "ee869f413c43",
     "text": "Yes — Animal Kingdom is one of the easiest Disney World parks for mixed-age families, because most of what it does best has no height requirement at all. Animal trails, a safari ride, a gentle boat ride, a train and live shows work for babies, preschoolers and grandparents alike. The trade-off is a shorter list of rides than Magic Kingdom, and only three attractions with a height minimum.",
     "marks": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "_type": "block",
   "_key": "e85ea0584520",
   "style": "normal",
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_type": "link",
     "_key": "cbd9816653f6",
     "href": "/rides/for/animal-kingdom-under-40/"
    }
   ],
   "children": [
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "c6107fde36d4",
     "text": "That makes height the first thing to check. Below, every current Animal Kingdom ride and major attraction is sorted by the official minimum height listed on Disney's attraction pages (checked October 16, 2026). Rules can change, so re-check close to your trip. Want the list filtered automatically? Open our ",
     "marks": []
    },
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "b2c64f953377",
     "text": "Animal Kingdom rides for kids under 40 inches",
     "marks": [
      "cbd9816653f6"
     ]
    },
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "c4043861e7a6",
     "text": " in the ride finder.",
     "marks": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "_type": "block",
   "_key": "74adcfc059f2",
   "style": "h2",
   "markDefs": [],
   "children": [
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "7e90e8acc750",
     "text": "Animal Kingdom Ride Heights at a Glance",
     "marks": []
    }
   ]
  },
