    },
    {
     "_type": "link",
     "_key": "f5e6b4910696",
     "href": "/blog/disney-world-with-baby-toddler/"
    }
   ],
   "children": [
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "9bed881fcc74",
     "text": "For many families, yes — especially as a lighter day between bigger parks. If your kids are mostly under 38 inches, Animal Kingdom gives them nearly full access. If your trip is short, compare it with the other parks in our ",
     "marks": []
    },
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "cc1d58cb7791",
     "text": "park chooser",
     "marks": [
      "4fe003103aa9"
     ]
    },
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "e66afb092fc3",
     "text": ", or read our ",
     "marks": []
    },
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "b122bf104395",
     "text": "Animal Kingdom park guide",
     "marks": [
      "b61b947e3fef"
     ]
    },
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "0a2f6e5f1f1a",
     "text": ". Families with babies may also like our ",
     "marks": []
    },
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "e539054663b9",
     "text": "Disney World with a baby or toddler guide",
     "marks": [
      "f5e6b4910696"
     ]
    },
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "306a1d5cfac3",
     "text": ".",
     "marks": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "_type": "block",
   "_key": "5005be185e2b",
   "style": "h2",
   "markDefs": [],
   "children": [
    {
     "_type": "span",
     "_key": "f6291151de75",
     "text": "Tickets",
